 "verdict": "include",
 "verdict_reason": "Own replication passes: SLB-rule labels from the 300k library are recovered by independent re-screens of the same lines at 0.73 (40k library, 29 pos; THP-1 0.82, Reh 0.66) and 0.76 (validation library, 36 pos; THP-1 0.80, Reh 0.71); reverse direction 0.62 / 0.87. Hit rate 0.48% (341/71,368), fitness-only AUROC 0.58-0.60. No same-line cross-study data exist, so no contradiction is possible under the rule; the pooled other-line comparison with included sources is 0.58 (20 pos), driven by non-paralog chromatin pairs measured only in SPIDR (RPE1, CRISPRi) - weak, different-line evidence, flagged. Caveat: the z-score is only reproducible in its extreme tail (Spearman 0.05-0.15 between libraries; 2%-tail split rule 0.53-0.59 vs 40k), so the -4 cut-off must not be loosened; z <= -5 replicates at 0.89-0.99 but gives only 63 positives (0.09%)."
}